// @@@ If the index is valid (greater than or equal to 0 and less than the current size of the vector), then for every valid index greater than the specified index and less than the old size minus one, the element at that index in the vector should either be null if the old element at the next index was null, or should be equal to the old element at the next index.
--------------------
// @@@ If the index is valid (greater than or equal to 0 and less than the current size of the vector), then for every index greater than the specified index and less than the previous size of the vector minus one, the element at each of these indices in the vector after the operation is either null and the old element at the next index was null, or it is equal to the old element at the next index.
--------------------
// @@@ if the index is valid (greater than or equal to 0 and less than the current size of the vector), then for every index greater than the specified index and less than the previous size minus one, the element at that index in the vector after the operation is either null and the corresponding old element was null, or it is equal to the element that was at the next higher index in the vector before the operation.
--------------------
